 <FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" ><B></b></font>
<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >Tell us about your family? Do you have any siblings? What are your parents like? etc...<br>
<br>
<br>
This is just another in a long series of posts that are directed at our getting to know each other better. I know not everyone's childhood was as Brady-esque as my own so only share what you are comfortable sharing, but do share something.<br>
<br>
I'll start:<br>
<br>
I am the oldest of three. I have a brother who is a year younger than me and a sister who is just shy of four years younger than me. Yes, that does mean she is tough as nails, she had no other choice. The relationship I have with both of them is good. We're all very different people, so we don't really hang out much. But that's alright, we get along and even like each other most of the time.<br>
<br>
As I said before, my upbringing was remarkably Brady-like. My parents are still married. Which is actually impressive considering that MoCo, Md has one of the highest divorce rates in the country and cops and teachers are two of the highest divorce rate professions. We had a dog, a cat, and some fish for a while. Although I was very angry at them for not being more open minded a few years ago (rebellious faze) that rebellion has moved on to acceptance and understanding. I understand now that I have never had anything to complain about. My parents are fair, loving, and very generous with their time and themselves. That's more than good enough for any kid.<br>
<br>
Anyway, that's a little about my family. What about you?</font></p>

