 <FONT face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" ><B></b></font>
<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >I have one brother and two step-sisters.  My brother is 15 years old, looks like a slightly shorter, slightly chubbier version of me, and often acts and thinks like me, though with slightly less wisdom in some cases.  We get along famously, and he's one of my best friends.  I think I've had more influence on him because of my parents being separated.  We would spend half the time at each house, but me and my brother were always at the same house together.<br>
<br>
My step sisters are 19 and 15-almost-16.  The older one and I get along pretty well, slightly better than I do with the younger one.  The older one has currently dropped out of college after a year and is now working a no-education job full time, and has moved out, though not officially.  The younger one has a bit of a self-esteem problem, gets too caught up in what other people think of her.  Can't stand her music (whatever's popular at the moment), or a big portion of her friends.<br>
<br>
My parents divorced in 1990, but live 4 miles away from each other, so our 50% custody was really that.  We'd spend 3 days at one house, 4 at the other, then the next week it would be 4 days and 3 respectively.<br>
<br>
My mom's personality is alot like mine, except less irreverent, a little closer to the status quo, and quite a bit more uptight about deadlines and such.  In the past few years, I've begun to see her as a normal person (as opposed to just a parent).  We usually get along pretty well, with occaisional arguements.<br>
<br>
My father is the less moral of my parents.  He's manipulative, lies when the truth will make him look bad (or when it suits him), but he's fairly smart.  He's not always pulling crap though.  He's very good at reading people, and uses the information he picks up to attract you to him.  He used to send me on horrible guilt trips whenever I did something bad, would punish me, then lift the punishment an hour later.  Once I realized the pattern, I usually sat stonily while he attempted to lay stuff on me, and tried not to think about that fact that my own father is trying to fuck with my head.  And the punishment was *still* lifted.  Despite this, I still managed to learn that negative actions have negative consequences.  Not too many people realize that alot of what my father says is BS, it takes awhile to learn.  The thing I'm most thankful to him for is my ability to smell BS and to read people, and for setting an example of how not to act.<br>
<br>
My step-mom ain't the brightest of folks.  Once told me The Fountainhead was a wonderful book (when she saw me reading it), and has extolled the virtues of socialism to me.  Those two events within an hour of each other.  She's hyper-sensitive to criticism, and this goes very bad with her lack of cooking skill.  "It's a little crispy" in a normal tone can send her up to the bedroom to sulk for the remainder of the day.  She and my father are in tremendous debt (he once told me "I don't live for the future, I want to enjoy the moment" when I pressed the issue), yet they haven't really done much to alleviate it.  The only thing saving them is the fact that my dad works alot of overtime, and gets paid well.<br>
<br>
We used to have a cocker spaniel at my mom's house, we have a terrier mutt and a poodle/duetschhound(sp?) mix at my dad's house now, a fat, genial white cat, a devilish obese gray cat, and a feral little long haired year old cat.  I've had an albino black rat snake, a euromastyx (it's a spiny desert lizard thing), a hamster, 2, then suddenly 6 guinea pigs, at least 50 fish (we had 3 tanks at one time) and a pet rock.<br>
<br>
Like Tanzit, I had a pretty good childhood.  Had self-esteem problems til about junior/senior high school year, but now I think I'm pretty psychologically healthy.   But hell, alot of people have major self-esteem problems their whole lives.<br>
<br>
I think I'm gonna do some more writing on this, help me map some stuff out.  Thanks Tanzit.<br>
__________________<br>
If there is a God, he is a malign thug. - Mark Twain</font></p>

