<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >I grew up in a small 3-bedroom home with my brothers Peter and Bobby, and my step-sisters Marcia, Jan, and Cindy.  We lived with our dad, Mike, and our step-mom Carol.  Our housekeeper, Alice, also lived with us.  She was a riot.  We had a dog named Tiger.  To most of the world, it seemed like I had an ideal childhood.  We would always have wacky stuff happen around the house, but we would always end up learning from it in the end.<br>
<br>
Things weren't always so keen, though.  Sometimes "mom" would come and play "games" with me and the boys in our room.  Peter and Bobby loved it, because they'd never had anyone do that to them before, but I knew what was up.  Especially after that one summer I spent givling Marcia.<br>
